    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n436" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ăcĕrātus</span></b> , a,
			um, adj.
		acus, ĕris, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>mingled with chaff</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">lutum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Fest. p. 20</span></i>
			, and 187 Müll.; cf. <i><span class="en">Non. 445,
				14</span></i>.</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			† <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ăcĕrătus</span></b> , a,
			um, adj., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀκέρατος</span>, <i>without horns</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">cochleae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					30, 6, 15, § 46</span></i>
			 dub. (acc. to others,
			ăcērătae = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀκήρατοι</span>, <i>complete</i>).</div>
